WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.440
I'm Russ Michaels with Tercet Law.

2
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.700
Most people think estate planning is about what happens after they're gone.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.040
But some of the most important papers are for while you're still here.

4
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.660
If a stroke, an accident, or a long illness means you can't make a decision

5
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.820
for a while, someone has to.

6
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.780
The question is who and whether you chose them.

7
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.380
A medical power of attorney names the person who makes healthcare decisions

8
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.260
with your doctors when you can't.

9
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.860
A durable power of attorney names the person who can pay your bills and

10
00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.740
handle your accounts.

11
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.140
Without them, your family may have to ask a court to appoint a guardian.

12
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.140
That can be slow, expensive, and public.

13
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:52.660
With them, the person you chose can step in without asking a judge first.

14
00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.940
I see this most with aging parents, a son or daughter who wants to help

15
00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.080
and can't because nothing was signed.

16
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.160
These are short documents.

17
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.640
They take an afternoon and they give the people you love permission to take

18
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.300
care of you.

19
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.500
There's a door here for you.

20
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.260
Click the link below and let's make sure the right person can speak for

21
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:14.480
you.

